WEBVTT

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:53.208
Is there a genetic match?

00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:56.478
Yes.
Let's gather the find

00:00:56.523 --> 00:00:58.354
and bring it back to the ship.

00:00:58.391 --> 00:01:00.951
Could this be it...
the proof?

00:01:00.994 --> 00:01:02.552
If it is, we've just made

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:05.086
the most important discovery
in Voth history.

00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:05.211
Opposable thumb.

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:07.617
Multiple articulations
in the digits...

00:03:07.654 --> 00:03:08.621
as expected with

00:03:08.655 --> 00:03:10.418
a technologically-advanced
species.

00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:24.294
Hmm... his cranial capacity
is 22 percent smaller than ours

00:03:24.337 --> 00:03:26.771
and he appears
to be lacking a dilitus lobe.

00:03:26.806 --> 00:03:29.070
He had no sense of smell?

00:03:29.108 --> 00:03:30.803
If he did, it was rudimentary.

00:03:30.843 --> 00:03:32.834
I doubt this fellow
would have enjoyed

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:34.471
the sulfur lagoons of Hokath.

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:39.376
His cartilaginous microstructure
is extremely porous.

00:03:39.419 --> 00:03:41.785
Most likely warm-blooded.

00:03:44.023 --> 00:03:46.583
I believe
this was a non-saurian.

00:03:46.626 --> 00:03:48.218
"Non-saurian"?

00:03:48.261 --> 00:03:50.161
Doesn't that weaken our case?

00:03:50.196 --> 00:03:52.824
No. No, the genetic markers

00:03:52.865 --> 00:03:54.389
we share with this being
are undeniable.

00:03:54.434 --> 00:03:56.561
We are related,
however distantly.

00:03:56.603 --> 00:03:59.094
The question we must answer is:

00:03:59.138 --> 00:04:01.936
What was our endotherm doing
in this part of space?

00:04:01.975 --> 00:04:04.773
Was he... on an expedition?

00:04:04.811 --> 00:04:07.177
Did he have a ship?
Crewmates?

00:04:09.282 --> 00:04:13.378
This material... it's composed
of synthetic polymers

00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:17.321
and the molecular structure
suggests replication technology.

00:04:17.357 --> 00:04:19.222
And consider
the garment itself...

00:04:19.259 --> 00:04:21.454
is this marking
purely decorative or does it

00:04:21.494 --> 00:04:22.961
have a symbolic function?

00:04:23.062 --> 00:04:24.620
Could it indicate status?

00:04:24.664 --> 00:04:27.189
Possibly a military uniform.

00:04:27.233 --> 00:04:28.700
At the very least, we can assume

00:04:28.735 --> 00:04:30.965
he was part
of a social infrastructure

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:33.061
and that would imply a ship.

00:04:43.616 --> 00:04:47.450
Did your eyes see
the planet of our origin?

00:04:47.487 --> 00:04:50.456
The true home of our race?

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:54.358
Was it... beautiful?

00:04:54.394 --> 00:04:57.693
Was it covered by oceans,
by sand?

00:04:57.730 --> 00:05:00.665
Were there nine moons
above your head?

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:02.190
Were there none?

00:05:05.438 --> 00:05:07.929
He appears to be
at a loss for words.

00:05:11.244 --> 00:05:12.734
His ship and the people on it

00:05:12.779 --> 00:05:14.542
hold the key
to where we came from.

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:15.945
We've got to find it.

00:05:16.049 --> 00:05:19.177
I'll contact our supporters
at the Circle of Archeology.

00:05:19.218 --> 00:05:21.243
They might be able
to spare a research vessel,

00:05:21.287 --> 00:05:22.379
perhaps a few assistants.

00:05:22.422 --> 00:05:24.390
This isn't a field trip, Veer.

00:05:24.424 --> 00:05:25.891
We need to mount
a sector-wide expedition.

00:05:25.925 --> 00:05:27.517
And that means a fleet of ships.

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:30.529
We have to go directly
to the Ministry of Elders.

00:05:30.563 --> 00:05:34.260
Professor, don't you think
that's a little precipitous?

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:37.531
Bone decalcification indicates
he died more than a year ago.

00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:40.061
His ship could be thousands
of light-years away by now.

00:05:40.106 --> 00:05:41.266
Time is running out.

00:05:41.307 --> 00:05:43.298
You must remember,
Veer, from the moment

00:05:43.343 --> 00:05:45.072
you were initiated
into my circle,

00:05:45.111 --> 00:05:46.339
you made a commitment

00:05:46.379 --> 00:05:48.472
to the pursuit
of scientific truth.

00:05:48.514 --> 00:05:50.982
Before this,
all we had was a theory.

00:05:51.084 --> 00:05:52.813
Now we have proof.

00:05:52.852 --> 00:05:55.912
We simply have to get them
to open their eyes and see it.

00:05:55.955 --> 00:05:58.583
We're going to set a course
for the city ship,

00:05:58.624 --> 00:06:02.287
present our friend here
and let him do the talking.

00:06:08.334 --> 00:06:11.030
For millions of years,
our people have believed

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:13.163
that we were
the first intelligent beings

00:06:13.206 --> 00:06:15.606
to evolve in this region
of space...

00:06:15.641 --> 00:06:17.939
the first race.

00:06:17.977 --> 00:06:18.944
This assumption

00:06:18.978 --> 00:06:21.469
underlies everything
that we hold dear.

00:06:21.514 --> 00:06:25.143
But that belief has been
questioned in recent years

00:06:25.184 --> 00:06:28.483
not only by the Circles
of Science and Philosophy

00:06:28.521 --> 00:06:30.853
but by common people as well.

00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:35.224
Lying before you is proof
of the Distant Origin Theory.

00:06:35.261 --> 00:06:37.695
These remains
demonstrate beyond doubt

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:40.221
that we arose elsewhere
in this galaxy,

00:06:40.266 --> 00:06:42.632
that we evolved
on a faraway planet

00:06:42.668 --> 00:06:45.899
and traveled to this space
millions of years ago,

00:06:45.938 --> 00:06:48.702
our true history lost.

00:06:48.741 --> 00:06:51.141
A pile of bones.

00:06:51.177 --> 00:06:53.111
Impressive.

00:06:53.146 --> 00:06:55.114
This "pile of bones"
belonged to a being

00:06:55.148 --> 00:06:57.548
who died
approximately one year ago

00:06:57.583 --> 00:07:00.848
from a species
found nowhere in known space.

00:07:00.887 --> 00:07:05.449
And yet, we share 47 genetic
markers with this being.

00:07:05.491 --> 00:07:08.187
We are undoubtedly
related to him.

00:07:08.227 --> 00:07:09.922
And I intend to prove to you

00:07:10.029 --> 00:07:12.930
that we evolved on
the very same planet he did.

00:07:12.999 --> 00:07:15.559
And that planet is
the long-lost world

00:07:15.601 --> 00:07:17.831
of the Distant Origin Theory.

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:20.065
Yes. That's exactly right.

00:07:20.106 --> 00:07:22.506
And to find that planet...

00:07:22.542 --> 00:07:24.407
our planet...

00:07:24.444 --> 00:07:27.038
we must find a living member
of his kind.

00:07:27.079 --> 00:07:29.912
I've created
a computer extrapolation.

00:07:29.949 --> 00:07:33.180
We're looking for a race
of bipedal endotherms...

00:07:33.219 --> 00:07:36.154
spacefaring,
but technologically limited.

00:07:36.189 --> 00:07:37.850
Based on their cranial capacity,

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:40.484
I'd say they're no more advanced
than most endotherms we've...

00:07:40.526 --> 00:07:41.515
"Endotherms"?

00:07:41.561 --> 00:07:42.528
You're proposing

00:07:42.562 --> 00:07:45.360
that we are related
to a mammalian species?

00:07:46.532 --> 00:07:47.658
Yes.

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:49.190
Which is why
I ask your permission

00:07:49.235 --> 00:07:50.634
to launch an expedition and...

00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:53.639
Let's talk about your discovery.

00:07:53.673 --> 00:07:59.578
I enjoyed the colorful tale
of how you found these remains.

00:07:59.612 --> 00:08:02.376
It says here that you
paid a substantial sum

00:08:02.415 --> 00:08:04.042
for their location.

00:08:04.083 --> 00:08:05.744
I was dealing with traders.

00:08:05.785 --> 00:08:07.275
They knew the location
of the cave.

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:08.378
I had no choice.

00:08:08.421 --> 00:08:11.185
Have you considered
you were the victim of a hoax?

00:08:11.224 --> 00:08:13.556
I have analyzed
every micron of this skeleton.

00:08:13.593 --> 00:08:15.083
I assure you, it's authentic.

00:08:15.127 --> 00:08:18.028
Professor Gegen,
have you considered

00:08:18.064 --> 00:08:21.727
the wider implications
of your... theory?

00:08:21.767 --> 00:08:22.859
What do you mean?

00:08:22.902 --> 00:08:24.563
By challenging Doctrine

00:08:24.604 --> 00:08:26.936
you're suggesting that
everything we believe

00:08:27.039 --> 00:08:29.735
about ourselves, our history,

00:08:29.775 --> 00:08:34.303
our ancient and rightful claim
over this region of space,

00:08:34.347 --> 00:08:38.340
the authority
of this Ministry itself...

00:08:38.384 --> 00:08:39.874
is a lie.

00:08:39.919 --> 00:08:42.319
That's not what I'm saying
at all.

00:08:42.355 --> 00:08:46.189
However, in the light
of my discovery,

00:08:46.225 --> 00:08:50.286
some of our beliefs
may have to be... reevaluated.

00:08:50.329 --> 00:08:53.196
"Reevaluated."

00:08:56.903 --> 00:09:02.671
We will... consider your
request for an expedition.

00:09:13.551 --> 00:09:15.542
Well done, Professor.

00:09:15.587 --> 00:09:17.179
Hardly.

00:09:17.222 --> 00:09:19.918
I failed to anticipate
the level of ignorance

00:09:19.991 --> 00:09:21.515
I would be facing.

00:09:21.559 --> 00:09:24.084
What do we do now?

00:09:24.128 --> 00:09:27.928
I want you to arrange a meeting
with the Circle of Exobiology.

00:09:28.032 --> 00:09:29.659
We have supporters there.

00:09:36.107 --> 00:09:39.474
Father, I'm concerned.

00:09:39.511 --> 00:09:40.773
Unnecessarily.

00:09:40.812 --> 00:09:43.110
I don't think
they were very receptive.

00:09:43.147 --> 00:09:44.341
They don't need to be.

00:09:44.382 --> 00:09:46.111
The evidence
will speak for itself

00:09:46.150 --> 00:09:49.142
and word of my discovery
is already traveling.

00:09:49.187 --> 00:09:50.677
If enough people
confront the Ministry...

00:09:50.722 --> 00:09:53.623
Mathematics was never
your strong point, Father.

00:09:53.658 --> 00:09:57.116
You might be overestimating
your support.

00:09:57.161 --> 00:09:58.958
You don't believe me,
either, do you?

00:09:59.030 --> 00:10:01.089
I...

00:10:01.132 --> 00:10:02.793
I want to.

00:10:04.536 --> 00:10:08.199
Our ancestors came
from somewhere else.

00:10:08.239 --> 00:10:11.299
We don't even belong here?

00:10:11.342 --> 00:10:15.142
It all just seems
so... incredible.

00:10:16.514 --> 00:10:18.311
I'm disappointed in you.

00:10:18.349 --> 00:10:21.477
Father, please...

00:10:21.519 --> 00:10:23.578
let this go.

00:10:23.621 --> 00:10:26.988
You're chasing a fantasy...

00:10:27.025 --> 00:10:29.220
and you're wasting
your genius.

00:10:31.396 --> 00:10:33.557
I'm worried about what's
going to happen to you

00:10:33.598 --> 00:10:34.587
if you don't stop.

00:10:34.632 --> 00:10:37.795
And what's going to happen
to you if I do stop?

00:10:37.835 --> 00:10:40.861
To your children,
to all of Voth?

00:10:40.905 --> 00:10:43.567
You'll continue
to live in ignorance...

00:10:43.608 --> 00:10:45.940
progress held back
by ancient myth.

00:10:45.977 --> 00:10:49.606
The truth must be known.

00:10:56.821 --> 00:10:58.584
We've got to leave...

00:10:58.623 --> 00:10:59.817
now.

00:10:59.857 --> 00:11:00.949
What's happened?

00:11:00.992 --> 00:11:02.960
I met
with the Circle of Exobiology.

00:11:02.994 --> 00:11:03.961
They're... concerned.

00:11:03.995 --> 00:11:04.962
There have been rumors.

00:11:04.996 --> 00:11:06.691
About what?

00:11:06.731 --> 00:11:08.130
The Ministry
has seized your research

00:11:08.166 --> 00:11:10.134
and they're planning
to detain you.

00:11:10.168 --> 00:11:11.760
On what charge?

00:11:11.803 --> 00:11:13.794
Heresy against Doctrine.

00:11:13.838 --> 00:11:15.066
I'll fight it.

00:11:15.106 --> 00:11:16.300
It's too late.

00:11:16.341 --> 00:11:17.603
Your supporters are frightened.

00:11:17.642 --> 00:11:18.631
No one will back you.

00:11:21.412 --> 00:11:23.972
I'll have to do this
on my own, then.

00:11:24.082 --> 00:11:26.744
Go back to your family.

00:11:26.784 --> 00:11:28.877
As long as you're with me,
you're at risk.

00:11:33.291 --> 00:11:35.350
I'm not leaving you, Professor.

00:11:39.063 --> 00:11:41.827
I've run an analysis
on the uniform marking.

00:11:41.866 --> 00:11:42.992
I found what appears

00:11:43.101 --> 00:11:45.501
to be a microscopic
identification code.

00:11:45.536 --> 00:11:49.768
The translation matrix indicates
it's most likely a proper name.

00:11:49.807 --> 00:11:50.933
A name?

00:11:50.975 --> 00:11:55.309
Yes. I believe it's the name
of the endotherm's vessel.

00:11:55.346 --> 00:11:57.143
We're looking
for something called...

00:11:58.149 --> 00:12:00.310
Voyager.

00:12:05.323 --> 00:12:06.790
Across the vastness of space

00:12:06.824 --> 00:12:09.224
to find one ship
among a sea of stars

00:12:09.260 --> 00:12:10.454
is no simple matter.

00:12:10.495 --> 00:12:13.589
And for many weeks,
we found nothing.

00:12:13.631 --> 00:12:16.464
And then, fortune glanced
in our direction.

00:12:16.501 --> 00:12:20.597
A trader from a space station
bordering the Nekrit Expanse

00:12:20.638 --> 00:12:23.368
informed us
of a curious group of explorers

00:12:23.408 --> 00:12:25.808
claiming to be from
the other side of the galaxy.

00:12:27.278 --> 00:12:29.974
The merchants there spoke
of a vessel called Voyager.

00:12:32.350 --> 00:12:35.842
They were able to help us
clarify certain details.

00:12:37.488 --> 00:12:38.921
With this new information,

00:12:38.956 --> 00:12:42.790
we began to acquire
other items and new evidence.

00:12:42.827 --> 00:12:45.159
Our most significant find:

00:12:45.196 --> 00:12:50.133
A canister of warp plasma
from Voyager's engines.

00:12:50.168 --> 00:12:53.331
So now we are scanning space
for a matching signature.

00:12:53.371 --> 00:12:55.601
Little is known
about these explorers,

00:12:55.640 --> 00:12:57.608
but they call themselves "human"

00:12:57.642 --> 00:12:59.269
and they claim
to be traveling home

00:12:59.310 --> 00:13:01.005
to a distant planet.

00:13:01.079 --> 00:13:03.274
My thoughts are with you, Frola,

00:13:03.314 --> 00:13:06.283
as are those
of my colleague, Veer.

00:13:06.317 --> 00:13:10.515
Ah, I just sent a transmission
to my daughter.

00:13:10.555 --> 00:13:12.386
Was that wise?

00:13:12.423 --> 00:13:13.913
I encrypted the carrier signal.

00:13:13.958 --> 00:13:15.289
There's no way to trace it.

00:13:15.326 --> 00:13:16.953
I hope you gave her my regards.

00:13:17.061 --> 00:13:18.323
Of course I did.

00:13:18.362 --> 00:13:20.956
I've seen the tint
on your scales

00:13:20.998 --> 00:13:22.659
when she's around.

00:13:22.700 --> 00:13:24.634
I've let you into
my academic circle,

00:13:24.669 --> 00:13:26.296
but now you wish to enter
my family as well?

00:13:26.337 --> 00:13:28.271
No, Professor,
I would never presume...

00:13:28.306 --> 00:13:29.796
You should know your place.

00:13:29.841 --> 00:13:33.368
Traditionally, my family mates
with the family of Towt.

00:13:38.015 --> 00:13:41.314
But... traditions are
meant to be broken.

00:13:46.224 --> 00:13:48.124
It's the plasma signature.

00:13:48.159 --> 00:13:53.290
Scanners have found a match...
a ship, 90 light-years away.

00:13:53.331 --> 00:13:55.390
There are 148 life-forms aboard,

00:13:55.433 --> 00:13:57.424
traveling at warp 6.2.

00:13:57.468 --> 00:13:59.368
I'm engaging
spatial displacement.

00:13:59.403 --> 00:14:01.371
It's unlikely
their primitive sensors

00:14:01.405 --> 00:14:04.169
will be able to detect us
once we're out of phase.

00:14:08.212 --> 00:14:09.543
Take us out of transwarp.

00:14:09.580 --> 00:14:10.774
We don't want to pass them.

00:14:10.815 --> 00:14:11.782
Done.

00:14:11.816 --> 00:14:13.784
I have an image.

00:14:13.818 --> 00:14:16.252
What do we say to them?

00:14:16.287 --> 00:14:18.687
Nothing.
Not at the moment.

00:14:18.723 --> 00:14:20.748
We stand to learn more
by observing them.

00:14:20.792 --> 00:14:23.317
Once we've collected
the information we need,

00:14:23.361 --> 00:14:26.762
and if they appear nonviolent,
we'll make contact.

00:14:28.032 --> 00:14:29.693
Entering portation range.

00:14:29.734 --> 00:14:32.294
We'll be looking for
their data storage devices,

00:14:32.336 --> 00:14:33.496
analyzing their behavior...

00:14:33.538 --> 00:14:36.473
anything that can tell us
who and what these people are.

00:14:36.507 --> 00:14:39.135
Eyes open, Veer.

00:14:50.354 --> 00:14:51.981
Interphase is stable.

00:14:52.089 --> 00:14:53.613
Curious.

00:14:53.658 --> 00:14:55.888
I didn't expect the smell.

00:14:55.927 --> 00:14:59.328
Well, they are mammals,
after all.

00:14:59.363 --> 00:15:00.990
Ah, over here.

00:15:04.502 --> 00:15:07.733
Ah, this appears to be
a computer access terminal.

00:15:07.772 --> 00:15:09.933
Simple binary system.

00:15:09.974 --> 00:15:13.068
I've downloaded their database.

00:15:13.110 --> 00:15:14.668
I'll bet you
it's an anodyne relay.

00:15:14.712 --> 00:15:15.701
No way. Plasma conduit.

00:15:15.746 --> 00:15:16.838
Relay.

00:15:16.881 --> 00:15:18.439
I'm telling you, I checked
the conduit network.

00:15:18.482 --> 00:15:19.744
My point exactly.

00:15:19.784 --> 00:15:21.183
You're not an engineer.

00:15:21.219 --> 00:15:22.379
I'll bet you.

00:15:22.420 --> 00:15:23.387
Name it.

00:15:23.421 --> 00:15:24.945
A male and female interacting.

00:15:24.989 --> 00:15:26.047
Let's observe.

00:15:32.129 --> 00:15:33.824
Well?

00:15:33.865 --> 00:15:36.561
Well...

00:15:36.601 --> 00:15:38.660
go ahead and gloat.

00:15:38.703 --> 00:15:41.797
The anodyne relays...
who would've guessed?

00:15:41.839 --> 00:15:42.965
Just a shot in the dark.

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:44.837
And it hit the bull's-eye.

00:15:44.876 --> 00:15:46.639
Tonight, you pay up.

00:15:46.677 --> 00:15:49.612
Holodeck 2, Klingon
martial arts program.

00:15:49.647 --> 00:15:51.205
No getting out of it this time.

00:15:51.249 --> 00:15:52.216
Courting behavior?

00:15:52.250 --> 00:15:53.740
Exactly.

00:15:53.784 --> 00:15:55.979
Note how the female,
through her feigned antagonism,

00:15:56.020 --> 00:15:58.614
encourages the male
in his attempt to mate.

00:15:58.656 --> 00:16:01.147
There's no sign of vasodilation
in their skin.

00:16:01.192 --> 00:16:03.717
Obviously, they never
evolved that ability,

00:16:03.761 --> 00:16:04.921
which would explain
their reliance

00:16:04.962 --> 00:16:06.930
on crude verbal interplay.

00:16:06.964 --> 00:16:08.158
I'll see you tonight.

00:16:08.199 --> 00:16:09.598
B.Y.O.B.

00:16:09.634 --> 00:16:10.726
What?

00:16:10.768 --> 00:16:13.168
Bring your own bat'leth.

00:16:16.540 --> 00:16:17.939
Bat'leth.

00:16:18.009 --> 00:16:19.306
Report.

00:16:19.343 --> 00:16:21.573
We've completed
long-range scans.

00:16:21.612 --> 00:16:23.842
If we maintain our present
course, we'll enter

00:16:23.881 --> 00:16:26.179
a region of heavy tetryon
radiation within two days.

00:16:26.217 --> 00:16:27.514
What's the alternative?

00:16:27.551 --> 00:16:28.916
A three-month detour.

00:16:28.953 --> 00:16:29.942
Tuvok, enhance the shields.

00:16:30.021 --> 00:16:31.318
Lieutenant, hold our course.

00:16:31.355 --> 00:16:32.947
Harry, continue
your long-range scans.

00:16:32.990 --> 00:16:34.048
Yes, ma'am.

00:16:34.091 --> 00:16:36.616
Let's access everything known
about tetryon radiation.

00:16:36.661 --> 00:16:38.219
I want to take
every precaution...

00:16:38.262 --> 00:16:41.095
Well, Veer, what can you observe
about their social structure?

00:16:41.132 --> 00:16:43.532
It's obviously hierarchical

00:16:43.567 --> 00:16:46.661
with clear differences
in status and rank.

00:16:46.704 --> 00:16:50.606
The males appear to be
subordinate to that female.

00:16:50.641 --> 00:16:53.303
Perhaps a matriarchy.

00:16:53.344 --> 00:16:55.335
My conclusion exactly.

00:16:56.380 --> 00:16:57.369
This is strange.

00:16:57.415 --> 00:16:59.781
I'm picking up
spatial fluctuations.

00:17:03.154 --> 00:17:05.054
They're coming from the Bridge.

00:17:05.089 --> 00:17:06.147
Source?

00:17:06.190 --> 00:17:08.249
I'm not sure,

00:17:08.292 --> 00:17:09.782
but they're highly localized

00:17:09.827 --> 00:17:12.762
with modulating phase variants.

00:17:12.797 --> 00:17:15.595
It looks like some kind
of cloaking technology.

00:17:15.633 --> 00:17:16.895
All stop.

00:17:16.934 --> 00:17:20.104
Intruder alert.

00:17:20.237 --> 00:17:21.636
We've exceeded our welcome.

00:17:21.672 --> 00:17:22.798
Let's get back to the ship.

00:17:24.374 --> 00:17:25.466
What's wrong?

00:17:25.509 --> 00:17:26.771
Some sort of force field.

00:17:26.810 --> 00:17:28.107
I've erected

00:17:28.145 --> 00:17:30.807
a level-10 containment field
around the Bridge, Captain.

00:17:30.848 --> 00:17:33.146
Scanning on all
subspace frequencies.

00:17:33.183 --> 00:17:35.048
I'm picking up two life-forms.

00:17:35.085 --> 00:17:37.212
Localize them.

00:17:37.254 --> 00:17:39.085
Mission Ops 1.

00:17:39.123 --> 00:17:40.351
Professor...

00:17:40.390 --> 00:17:42.620
Their force field
is disrupting our interphase.

00:17:42.659 --> 00:17:43.887
I'm compensating.

00:17:43.927 --> 00:17:46.418
I can at least get us
off this deck.

00:17:46.463 --> 00:17:47.794
Show yourselves.

00:17:47.831 --> 00:17:50.129
Captain, the life-forms
left the Bridge.

00:17:50.167 --> 00:17:53.728
They're now on Deck 2,
Section 13, Mess Hall.

00:17:53.770 --> 00:17:54.930
Seal off the deck.

00:17:54.972 --> 00:17:56.405
Deck 2 sealed.

00:17:56.440 --> 00:17:57.998
Security team to the Mess Hall.

00:17:59.143 --> 00:18:01.771
Intruders?
I don't see any intruders.

00:18:01.812 --> 00:18:05.043
It would appear we've
underestimated our endotherms.

00:18:05.082 --> 00:18:06.674
Maybe we should make contact...

00:18:06.717 --> 00:18:07.706
explain ourselves.

00:18:07.751 --> 00:18:08.877
It may come to that.

00:18:08.919 --> 00:18:09.908
Captain,

00:18:09.953 --> 00:18:11.921
I've analyzed those
spatial phase variants.

00:18:12.022 --> 00:18:13.649
Bridge to Chakotay.

00:18:13.690 --> 00:18:14.657
Go ahead.

00:18:14.691 --> 00:18:16.056
Adjust hand phasers

00:18:16.093 --> 00:18:18.823
to a dispersion frequency
of 1.85 gigahertz.

00:18:18.862 --> 00:18:20.921
That should disrupt
their cloaking technology.

00:18:20.964 --> 00:18:22.556
Acknowledged.

00:18:22.599 --> 00:18:24.624
I've matched the frequency
of their shields.

00:18:24.668 --> 00:18:26.101
I think we can get off this...

00:18:33.310 --> 00:18:35.835
Spatial fluctuations...

00:18:35.879 --> 00:18:36.846
there.

00:18:36.880 --> 00:18:37.778
Neelix, get down!

00:19:12.983 --> 00:19:15.577
Minor phaser burns
to the upper thoracic region...

00:19:15.619 --> 00:19:16.643
nothing serious...

00:19:16.687 --> 00:19:18.314
but I want to check
for cellular damage.

00:19:18.355 --> 00:19:19.617
I'll run a microcellular scan.

00:19:19.656 --> 00:19:21.624
Begin a DNA analysis as well.

00:19:21.658 --> 00:19:23.785
I'd like to know more
about his molecular physiology.

00:19:23.827 --> 00:19:25.488
A belated welcome aboard.

00:19:25.529 --> 00:19:26.928
I'm Captain Janeway.

00:19:26.964 --> 00:19:28.522
Now, who are you
and what have you done

00:19:28.565 --> 00:19:29.725
with my First Officer?

00:19:32.002 --> 00:19:33.401
You must have a ship.

00:19:33.437 --> 00:19:34.404
Is it cloaked?

00:19:37.274 --> 00:19:38.366
We're not going to hurt you.

00:19:38.408 --> 00:19:41.104
We just want to know why you...

00:19:42.246 --> 00:19:44.578
His heart rate and body
temperature have dropped.

00:19:44.615 --> 00:19:47.175
His metabolism is almost
completely shut down.

00:19:47.217 --> 00:19:48.343
Is he dying?

00:19:48.385 --> 00:19:49.545
I don't think so.

00:19:49.586 --> 00:19:51.952
His autonomic nervous system
is still fully functional.

00:19:52.022 --> 00:19:55.185
He's gone into some sort
of protective hibernation.

00:19:55.225 --> 00:19:57.853
Treat his injuries,
then see if you can revive him.

00:19:57.894 --> 00:19:59.794
Examine his technology.

00:19:59.830 --> 00:20:01.627
I want to know
what we're up against.

00:20:11.842 --> 00:20:13.571
Don't be alarmed.

00:20:13.610 --> 00:20:15.976
You're on my research vessel.

00:20:16.046 --> 00:20:17.445
Chakotay to Voyager.

00:20:17.481 --> 00:20:18.539
Your instinct is to flee,

00:20:18.582 --> 00:20:20.675
but I must warn you
there's a confinement field

00:20:20.717 --> 00:20:21.979
around the table.

00:20:22.085 --> 00:20:23.950
Just stay calm and you
won't hurt yourself.

00:20:25.889 --> 00:20:27.754
What do you want from me?

00:20:27.791 --> 00:20:29.156
Why did you invade our ship?

00:20:29.192 --> 00:20:31.183
It wasn't an invasion.

00:20:31.228 --> 00:20:33.753
We were on a field expedition
to learn more

00:20:33.797 --> 00:20:35.230
about your species.

00:20:35.265 --> 00:20:37.096
We meant no harm.

00:20:37.134 --> 00:20:39.295
I'm a molecular paleontologist.

00:20:39.336 --> 00:20:41.634
Do you always harpoon
the local wildlife?

00:20:41.672 --> 00:20:44.197
An unfortunate mistake.

00:20:44.241 --> 00:20:47.005
Veer is inexperienced,
and he panicked.

00:20:47.077 --> 00:20:49.136
Your people were firing at us.

00:20:49.179 --> 00:20:50.669
I couldn't get to him.

00:20:50.714 --> 00:20:52.841
So you took me instead.

00:20:52.883 --> 00:20:54.942
Yes.
A living specimen of human.

00:20:54.985 --> 00:20:58.443
I've been studying
your computer database

00:20:58.488 --> 00:21:00.854
and I have many questions.

00:21:00.891 --> 00:21:04.122
The planet of your origin,
correct?

00:21:04.161 --> 00:21:06.322
That's right. Earth.

00:21:08.332 --> 00:21:11.733
Are there any of my kind there?

00:21:11.768 --> 00:21:14.066
Any of my species?

00:21:14.104 --> 00:21:15.731
Who are you?

00:21:15.772 --> 00:21:17.740
Please, answer the question.

00:21:17.774 --> 00:21:21.403
Look, drop the force field
and tell me what's going on.

00:21:21.445 --> 00:21:24.676
Then, maybe we can make first
contact in a civilized way.

00:21:24.715 --> 00:21:26.740
For what it's worth,
I'm a scientist, too.

00:21:26.783 --> 00:21:27.977
Maybe I can help you find

00:21:28.018 --> 00:21:29.713
whatever it is
you're looking for.

00:21:29.753 --> 00:21:31.152
I won't bite.

00:21:36.493 --> 00:21:38.154
Thanks.

00:21:40.263 --> 00:21:41.753
My name's Chakotay.

00:21:41.798 --> 00:21:43.595
Gegen.

00:21:43.633 --> 00:21:47.399
All right, Gegen,
let's talk about Earth.

00:21:52.409 --> 00:21:53.671
Your call sounded urgent.

00:21:53.710 --> 00:21:54.904
With good reason.

00:21:54.945 --> 00:21:56.879
I've analyzed the alien's DNA.

00:21:56.913 --> 00:21:58.608
There are 47 genetic markers

00:21:58.648 --> 00:22:00.809
identical to those found
in human DNA.

00:22:00.851 --> 00:22:01.909
That's more than coincidence.

00:22:01.952 --> 00:22:02.941
I thought so, too.

00:22:03.019 --> 00:22:04.680
I ran a search for those markers

00:22:04.721 --> 00:22:06.655
in Earth's
paleontological database.

00:22:06.690 --> 00:22:08.351
Take a look at this.

00:22:10.627 --> 00:22:11.616
Incredible.

00:22:11.661 --> 00:22:13.185
That's one way of putting it.

00:22:13.230 --> 00:22:15.357
It says here that those markers
appeared in hundreds

00:22:15.399 --> 00:22:19.301
of Earth species, dating back
tens of millions of...

00:22:23.073 --> 00:22:25.200
Their species evolved on Earth?

00:22:25.242 --> 00:22:27.073
Apparently so.

00:22:27.110 --> 00:22:30.944
And from the look of it,
you and he are distant cousins.

00:22:30.981 --> 00:22:33.211
I wonder how distant.

00:22:33.250 --> 00:22:35.946
Transfer yourself to Holodeck 2.

00:22:35.986 --> 00:22:37.476
I think it's time
we took a stroll

00:22:37.521 --> 00:22:39.216
through primeval history.

00:22:43.260 --> 00:22:45.922
I've entered the genetic markers
into the holo-database.

00:22:45.962 --> 00:22:48.795
Let's see if we can find
our closet relative.

00:22:48.832 --> 00:22:50.925
Computer, analyze
the genetic markers

00:22:50.967 --> 00:22:52.992
and search Earth's
fossil record.

00:22:53.036 --> 00:22:55.300
Identify any ancestors
common to both humans

00:22:55.338 --> 00:22:57.499
and the alien in Sick Bay.

00:22:57.541 --> 00:22:59.304
Life-form found.

00:22:59.342 --> 00:23:00.809
Display.

00:23:00.844 --> 00:23:02.277
Genus eryops.

00:23:02.312 --> 00:23:04.337
Devonian Era.

00:23:04.381 --> 00:23:05.939
Eryops...

00:23:06.016 --> 00:23:08.849
this creature lived
over 400 million years ago.

00:23:08.885 --> 00:23:12.377
And is thought to be
the last common ancestor

00:23:12.422 --> 00:23:14.856
of cold-blooded and
warm-blooded organisms.

00:23:14.891 --> 00:23:15.858
Yes, yes.

00:23:15.892 --> 00:23:18.622
Let's take the next step
in our little stroll.

00:23:18.662 --> 00:23:20.527
Computer, what's
the most highly evolved

00:23:20.564 --> 00:23:23.965
cold-blooded organism
to develop from the eryops?

00:23:24.000 --> 00:23:27.527
Genus hadrosaur.
Cretaceous Era.

00:23:27.571 --> 00:23:29.596
Display the life-form.

00:23:33.510 --> 00:23:36.570
As I recall,
the hadrosaur vanished

00:23:36.613 --> 00:23:38.137
when a mass extinction occurred

00:23:38.181 --> 00:23:41.173
at the end
of the Cretaceous Period.

00:23:42.519 --> 00:23:44.646
What if the hadrosaur
didn't die off?

00:23:44.688 --> 00:23:47.350
What if some of them
survived that extinction

00:23:47.390 --> 00:23:49.449
and continued to evolve?

00:23:49.493 --> 00:23:51.290
I could well imagine
this creature

00:23:51.328 --> 00:23:53.956
giving rise to a more
complex life-form.

00:23:53.997 --> 00:23:56.864
Certainly the building blocks
are there...

00:23:56.900 --> 00:23:59.801
bipedal, grasping hands...

00:23:59.836 --> 00:24:03.237
Computer, run a genome
projection algorithm.

00:24:03.273 --> 00:24:06.265
If the hadrosaur
had continued to evolve

00:24:06.309 --> 00:24:08.709
over the last 65 million years,

00:24:08.745 --> 00:24:11.509
extrapolate the most probable
appearance.

00:24:11.548 --> 00:24:12.947
Extrapolation complete.

00:24:13.049 --> 00:24:14.141
Display life-form.

00:24:18.788 --> 00:24:20.847
That creature napping
in Sick Bay...

00:24:20.891 --> 00:24:22.518
is a dinosaur.

00:24:22.559 --> 00:24:24.288
The question is:

00:24:25.829 --> 00:24:30.967
Why have we never seen him
in the natural history museums?

00:24:31.100 --> 00:24:32.761
If a saurian species
had developed

00:24:32.802 --> 00:24:34.360
a language and technology,

00:24:34.403 --> 00:24:36.530
you'd think they would have
left something behind,

00:24:36.572 --> 00:24:39.769
but what if it evolved
on an isolated continent?

00:24:39.809 --> 00:24:42.107
A land mass that was destroyed.

00:24:42.144 --> 00:24:45.079
Earth has been devastated
by countless natural disasters

00:24:45.114 --> 00:24:47.981
over the course of its history...
asteroids, volcanoes,

00:24:48.084 --> 00:24:49.142
earthquakes.

00:24:49.185 --> 00:24:50.982
All evidence of your race
could be

00:24:51.020 --> 00:24:54.217
at the bottom of the ocean
or under kilometers of rock.

00:24:54.256 --> 00:24:56.690
Obviously, not all of my people
became extinct.

00:24:56.726 --> 00:24:59.160
Some of them must have developed
space-faring technology

00:24:59.195 --> 00:25:00.856
and left the planet.

00:25:00.896 --> 00:25:03.262
And ended up here
in the Delta Quadrant.

00:25:03.299 --> 00:25:06.700
Our true origins on Earth
lost over the eons,

00:25:06.736 --> 00:25:09.034
replaced by Doctrine...

00:25:09.071 --> 00:25:11.437
the myth that we were
the first race.

00:25:13.209 --> 00:25:16.235
Now you understand
why I had to find your ship.

00:25:16.278 --> 00:25:19.645
Next time, you might try
a simple "hello" first.

00:25:21.217 --> 00:25:23.276
"Eyes open."

00:25:23.319 --> 00:25:26.777
I'm afraid I let my own
prejudice get in the way.

00:25:26.822 --> 00:25:30.349
I was... wary of you.

00:25:30.393 --> 00:25:33.794
We have very poor relations
with non-saurian races.

00:25:33.829 --> 00:25:37.356
Mammals in particular
are considered to be a...

00:25:37.400 --> 00:25:39.095
lower life-form,

00:25:39.135 --> 00:25:42.332
but I must admit, I've never
gotten to know one before.

00:25:42.371 --> 00:25:44.100
I hope I've made
a good impression.

00:25:44.140 --> 00:25:46.631
In fact, you have.

00:25:46.675 --> 00:25:49.075
Well, I suggest we
get back to Voyager.

00:25:49.111 --> 00:25:50.840
Your friend Veer
is probably sick

00:25:50.880 --> 00:25:52.472
of the mammalian food by now.

00:25:52.515 --> 00:25:53.982
I can't do that.

00:25:54.016 --> 00:25:55.313
Why not?

00:25:55.351 --> 00:25:56.648
I've already made arrangements

00:25:56.685 --> 00:25:58.516
to meet my supporters
on the fourth colony.

00:25:58.554 --> 00:25:59.578
They're waiting for us.

00:25:59.622 --> 00:26:01.146
Tell them we'll be late.

00:26:01.190 --> 00:26:02.782
You don't understand
what I'm up against.

00:26:02.825 --> 00:26:05.419
I'm being charged
with heresy against Doctrine.

00:26:05.461 --> 00:26:06.758
You're my only evidence.

00:26:06.796 --> 00:26:09.458
If enough people see
living proof of my theory,

00:26:09.498 --> 00:26:12.763
even the Ministry will be forced
to acknowledge the truth.

00:26:12.802 --> 00:26:15.464
I can't let you go now.

00:26:15.504 --> 00:26:17.938
Not until it's over.

00:26:18.040 --> 00:26:19.029
I'm sorry.

00:26:21.143 --> 00:26:22.838
This should to the trick.

00:26:25.047 --> 00:26:26.537
An apple?

00:26:26.582 --> 00:26:29.073
You said you wanted
an organic test subject.

00:26:29.118 --> 00:26:31.450
I was referring
to a bio-cylinder,

00:26:31.487 --> 00:26:33.216
but the fruit will suffice.

00:26:33.255 --> 00:26:35.382
Let's give it a try.

00:26:37.993 --> 00:26:39.187
Fascinating.

00:26:39.228 --> 00:26:41.856
This alien device is apparently
pushing the apple

00:26:41.897 --> 00:26:44.559
slightly out of phase
with our space-time continuum.

00:26:44.600 --> 00:26:46.966
A personal cloaking device.

00:26:47.069 --> 00:26:50.596
More advanced than any cloak
I've ever seen.

00:26:52.074 --> 00:26:53.405
Mr. Kim?

00:26:53.442 --> 00:26:56.502
I'm reading a massive spatial
displacement dead ahead.

00:27:01.917 --> 00:27:03.077
Red Alert.

00:27:04.453 --> 00:27:05.420
We're being probed.

00:27:05.454 --> 00:27:06.716
Shields at maximum.

00:27:06.755 --> 00:27:08.120
Hail them.

00:27:08.157 --> 00:27:10.489
No response.

00:27:10.526 --> 00:27:13.927
They're locking onto the ship
with an energy beam.

00:27:14.029 --> 00:27:15.724
It's cutting right through
our shields.

00:27:15.764 --> 00:27:18.324
It's some sort of transporter.

00:27:27.376 --> 00:27:28.400
Report.

00:27:28.444 --> 00:27:30.844
We've been beamed
inside the alien vessel.

00:27:43.859 --> 00:27:44.848
We're losing power.

00:27:44.894 --> 00:27:45.952
Switch to auxiliary.

00:27:46.028 --> 00:27:48.223
I'm locked out
of command control.

00:27:48.264 --> 00:27:49.891
All systems are shutting down.

00:27:53.802 --> 00:27:55.633
Arm yourselves.

00:27:57.773 --> 00:27:59.331
Tuvok to Bridge.

00:27:59.375 --> 00:28:01.434
Captain Janeway, respond.

00:28:11.086 --> 00:28:13.020
Turbolifts are off-line.

00:28:13.055 --> 00:28:14.522
Let's get to a Jefferies tube.

00:28:23.699 --> 00:28:26.167
Tuvok, I hope
that's your stomach.

00:28:34.643 --> 00:28:36.668
My tricorder's not working.

00:28:36.712 --> 00:28:38.703
There appears
to be a dampening fie...

00:28:39.715 --> 00:28:40.909
Tuvok?

00:28:47.890 --> 00:28:48.857
Go.

00:28:48.891 --> 00:28:49.858
I'm not going to...

00:28:49.892 --> 00:28:51.086
That's an order, Lieutenant.

00:28:58.867 --> 00:29:01.597
I can't get a single relay
back on-line.

00:29:01.637 --> 00:29:03.502
Somehow, they've locked us
out of all primary systems.

00:29:03.539 --> 00:29:04.665
Let's get down
to Main Engineering.

00:29:04.707 --> 00:29:06.265
We can access the manual
override from there...

00:29:10.946 --> 00:29:13.676
Your vessel
is under our control.

00:29:20.289 --> 00:29:22.723
It's an automated message
from the Ministry of Elders.

00:29:22.758 --> 00:29:25.818
It says that they've
captured the Voyager,

00:29:25.861 --> 00:29:27.852
that if I don't return
to the city ship

00:29:27.896 --> 00:29:31.457
and face my accusers,
they'll destroy my evidence...

00:29:31.500 --> 00:29:33.627
kill everyone on board.

00:29:36.138 --> 00:29:37.867
What are you going to do?

00:29:37.906 --> 00:29:40.101
I won't be responsible
for those deaths,

00:29:40.142 --> 00:29:43.669
but if I go back now
without my support,

00:29:43.712 --> 00:29:47.045
they'll discredit my theory;
suppress the truth.

00:29:48.050 --> 00:29:48.948
That might be difficult

00:29:49.051 --> 00:29:50.916
with the evidence
standing right beside you.

00:29:50.953 --> 00:29:53.251
They've taken my ship.

00:29:53.289 --> 00:29:55.723
It sounds to me
like we're all on trial here.

00:29:59.662 --> 00:30:02.563
I've just laid in a course
for the city ship.

00:30:05.968 --> 00:30:08.368
We're looking
for two of our own kind.

00:30:08.404 --> 00:30:10.702
One was found
in your medical bay.

00:30:10.739 --> 00:30:11.706
Where is the other?

00:30:11.740 --> 00:30:12.707
I don't know.

00:30:12.741 --> 00:30:14.936
He took my First Officer
and disappeared.

00:30:14.977 --> 00:30:17.502
Our scans indicate
that your ship is alone.

00:30:17.546 --> 00:30:19.309
Where do you come from?

00:30:19.348 --> 00:30:21.373
If you want my cooperation,

00:30:21.417 --> 00:30:23.749
I suggest you release my vessel.

00:30:23.786 --> 00:30:25.447
You are non-indigenous beings.

00:30:25.487 --> 00:30:27.717
You have no rights
under Doctrine.

00:30:27.756 --> 00:30:30.156
Where do you come from?

00:30:30.192 --> 00:30:34.128
Apparently... we're from
the same place you are...

00:30:34.163 --> 00:30:35.790
Earth.

00:30:37.700 --> 00:30:41.636
I see that Gegen
has begun spreading his lies.

00:31:13.102 --> 00:31:14.831
Paris to Janeway.

00:31:14.870 --> 00:31:18.067
Captain, if you can hear me,
I've got weapons control

00:31:18.107 --> 00:31:20.974
and I've armed
a full spread of torpedoes.

00:31:21.009 --> 00:31:21.976
Who's that?

00:31:22.077 --> 00:31:23.203
My helmsman.

00:31:23.245 --> 00:31:25.839
Sounds like he's
about to blast a hole

00:31:25.881 --> 00:31:27.439
in the side of your ship.

00:31:27.483 --> 00:31:29.246
Lieutenant Paris, fire.

00:31:29.284 --> 00:31:31.149
You might want
to hold on to something.

00:31:35.090 --> 00:31:37.923
Launch protocols
have been disrupted.

00:31:37.960 --> 00:31:40.952
Switch to auxiliary protocols.

00:31:40.996 --> 00:31:42.987
Unable to comply.

00:31:43.031 --> 00:31:45.295
Weapon systems are off-line.

00:31:45.334 --> 00:31:46.665
How?

00:31:46.702 --> 00:31:48.329
Method unknown.

00:31:49.838 --> 00:31:50.998
Paris to Janeway.

00:31:51.106 --> 00:31:52.232
Go ahead.

00:31:52.274 --> 00:31:53.707
Captain, someone
on the alien vessel

00:31:53.742 --> 00:31:55.710
detected my launch sequence.

00:31:55.744 --> 00:31:58.110
I don't know how they did it,
but I'm completely locked out.

00:31:58.147 --> 00:31:59.876
Nice try, Tom.

00:31:59.915 --> 00:32:01.610
Haluk to Command.

00:32:01.650 --> 00:32:04.210
The Voyager's Captain
is proving uncooperative.

00:32:04.253 --> 00:32:06.915
I request an interrogation
surgeon to assist with the...

00:32:06.955 --> 00:32:08.081
That won't be necessary.

00:32:08.123 --> 00:32:09.454
Gegen is in custody.

00:32:09.491 --> 00:32:10.617
Remain on the Voyager

00:32:10.659 --> 00:32:12.126
and wait
for further instructions.

00:32:25.507 --> 00:32:27.975
Professor Forra Gegen,

00:32:28.043 --> 00:32:31.069
you are accused
of heresy against Doctrine.

00:32:31.113 --> 00:32:33.604
Do you wish
to retract your claims

00:32:33.649 --> 00:32:36.311
regarding
the Distant Origin Theory?

00:32:36.351 --> 00:32:38.649
I do not.

00:32:42.724 --> 00:32:45.215
Then we will proceed.

00:32:50.198 --> 00:32:52.894
Three months ago,
you circulated a study

00:32:52.934 --> 00:32:56.370
criticizing what you called
"resistance to truth"...

00:32:56.404 --> 00:32:58.599
once again, disputing Doctrine.

00:32:58.640 --> 00:33:01.734
I apologize if I wrote anything
that offended the Elders,

00:33:01.776 --> 00:33:04.609
but I never even mentioned
the word "doctrine."

00:33:04.646 --> 00:33:06.443
You didn't have to.

00:33:06.481 --> 00:33:08.472
Your meaning was clear.

00:33:08.516 --> 00:33:10.211
For nearly a decade,

00:33:10.251 --> 00:33:12.344
you've used
the Distant Origin Theory

00:33:12.387 --> 00:33:13.945
to attack and undermine

00:33:13.988 --> 00:33:16.388
the guiding principles
of our society.

00:33:16.424 --> 00:33:19.723
Not so! I've been pursuing
a scientific investigation.

00:33:19.761 --> 00:33:21.592
I'm not concerned at all
with Doctrine!

00:33:21.629 --> 00:33:23.529
My point exactly.

00:33:23.565 --> 00:33:26.966
Your disregard for the effects
of your casual theorizing

00:33:27.035 --> 00:33:28.900
is why you stand accused.

00:33:28.937 --> 00:33:31.929
You are reckless
and irresponsible, and you are

00:33:31.973 --> 00:33:34.635
a destructive influence
to our society.

00:33:34.676 --> 00:33:36.109
But it is not too late

00:33:36.144 --> 00:33:38.669
for you to redress
the damage you have done.

00:33:38.713 --> 00:33:40.578
Disavow your claims.

00:33:40.615 --> 00:33:42.105
Acknowledge your mistakes

00:33:42.150 --> 00:33:44.812
and this Ministry
will show you leniency.

00:33:44.853 --> 00:33:46.650
I'm sorry.

00:33:46.688 --> 00:33:48.986
I can't deny the evidence.

00:33:49.090 --> 00:33:51.285
The proof is standing
right beside me.

00:33:51.326 --> 00:33:52.816
Proof?

00:33:52.861 --> 00:33:54.089
Really?

00:33:54.129 --> 00:33:57.530
Our scientists have
analyzed your data.

00:33:57.565 --> 00:33:58.998
Their conclusion:

00:33:59.033 --> 00:34:01.831
"These creatures are
not related to us at all.

00:34:01.870 --> 00:34:03.064
"The genetic similarities

00:34:03.104 --> 00:34:07.404
are a result of random
convergence, nothing more."

00:34:07.442 --> 00:34:08.807
If I may speak?

00:34:10.345 --> 00:34:11.937
Voyager's database contains

00:34:12.046 --> 00:34:14.640
a complete fossil record
of my planet.

00:34:14.682 --> 00:34:17.583
Your genetic markers appear
not only in humans

00:34:17.619 --> 00:34:20.247
but in hundreds of species
throughout our history.

00:34:20.288 --> 00:34:22.950
That's a lot
of "random convergence."

00:34:23.024 --> 00:34:24.958
If you'd take a look
at the data...

00:34:25.026 --> 00:34:26.152
We have.

00:34:26.194 --> 00:34:28.219
The data isn't in question.

00:34:28.263 --> 00:34:31.426
Your interpretation is.

00:34:31.466 --> 00:34:34.162
Professor Gegen,
I don't want to be here

00:34:34.202 --> 00:34:35.863
any more than you do,

00:34:35.904 --> 00:34:39.135
and frankly, I would prefer
not to be responsible

00:34:39.174 --> 00:34:43.338
for disgracing one of
our most venerable scientists.

00:34:43.378 --> 00:34:46.142
All I ask is that
you admit the possibility

00:34:46.181 --> 00:34:48.741
that your interpretation
is wrong.

00:34:48.783 --> 00:34:50.978
Will you at least do that?

00:34:51.052 --> 00:34:54.920
I will admit that there
are still questions.

00:34:54.956 --> 00:34:56.981
The picture is incomplete.

00:34:57.058 --> 00:34:59.891
But I am certain of this:

00:34:59.928 --> 00:35:04.331
We are from the planet
these humans call Earth.

00:35:04.365 --> 00:35:06.890
There are those who disagree.

00:35:20.181 --> 00:35:24.481
Tova Veer, you are
an accomplished young scientist.

00:35:24.519 --> 00:35:26.919
You were initiated
into the Circle of Archaeology

00:35:26.955 --> 00:35:28.889
with the highest of honors.

00:35:28.923 --> 00:35:30.356
Yes, Minister.

00:35:30.391 --> 00:35:33.952
And you have been Professor
Gegen's assistant for six years.

00:35:34.062 --> 00:35:35.893
I've had that privilege.

00:35:35.930 --> 00:35:37.761
You are familiar...

00:35:37.799 --> 00:35:41.257
intimately involved with
all of your mentor's research

00:35:41.302 --> 00:35:44.396
regarding the so-called
Distant Origin Theory?

00:35:44.439 --> 00:35:45.701
That is correct.

00:35:45.740 --> 00:35:48.470
In your expert evaluation,

00:35:48.509 --> 00:35:52.673
what is the validity
of the Professor's analysis?

00:35:56.017 --> 00:35:58.212
It is flawed, Minister.

00:35:58.253 --> 00:35:59.049
Veer!

00:36:00.121 --> 00:36:03.249
You're saying you and Gegen
were mistaken?

00:36:05.293 --> 00:36:07.056
Yes.

00:36:07.095 --> 00:36:09.154
I've reviewed
all of his research,

00:36:09.197 --> 00:36:12.826
including data
from the Voyager's computer.

00:36:12.867 --> 00:36:16.268
I've checked and rechecked
the procedures.

00:36:16.304 --> 00:36:20.604
I now believe
that we were... overzealous.

00:36:20.642 --> 00:36:23.270
We saw an evolutionary
connection

00:36:23.311 --> 00:36:25.245
when, in fact, there was none.

00:36:25.280 --> 00:36:28.772
Enthusiasm and passion
are never wrong, Veer.

00:36:28.816 --> 00:36:32.411
Your only mistake was allowing
them to distort your judgment.

00:36:32.453 --> 00:36:34.387
You may go.

00:36:38.793 --> 00:36:42.456
Professor Gegen,
I will ask you again:

00:36:42.497 --> 00:36:44.590
Could you be mistaken?

00:36:44.632 --> 00:36:46.293
What did you say to him?

00:36:46.334 --> 00:36:49.963
That you'd take away his honors
if he didn't cooperate?

00:36:50.004 --> 00:36:53.462
That you'd send him
to a detention colony?

00:36:53.508 --> 00:36:55.271
Could you be mistaken?

00:36:55.310 --> 00:36:56.641
Did you threaten his family?!

00:36:56.678 --> 00:36:57.906
Respond to the question!

00:36:57.946 --> 00:36:59.607
No! Why should I?

00:36:59.647 --> 00:37:01.342
You've already made up
your mind.

00:37:01.382 --> 00:37:03.680
This inquiry isn't
about evidence and proof.

00:37:03.718 --> 00:37:05.310
It's about keeping you
in that chair!

00:37:05.353 --> 00:37:06.320
Gegen!

00:37:06.354 --> 00:37:07.787
It's about maintaining a myth

00:37:07.822 --> 00:37:09.483
that keeps the Ministry
in power.

00:37:09.524 --> 00:37:11.924
You'd do anything to silence me.

00:37:12.026 --> 00:37:13.926
Well, it won't work.

00:37:14.028 --> 00:37:15.791
I'll never retract my claims.

00:37:15.830 --> 00:37:17.263
I'd rather go to prison

00:37:17.298 --> 00:37:19.459
than help you
perpetuate ignorance!

00:37:19.500 --> 00:37:22.936
Your true scales
are finally showing.

00:37:23.037 --> 00:37:25.164
You're right, Minister.

00:37:25.206 --> 00:37:27.071
I was mistaken.

00:37:27.108 --> 00:37:30.771
I thought you might actually
care about the truth,

00:37:30.812 --> 00:37:32.404
even if it called into question

00:37:32.447 --> 00:37:34.677
some of our deepest beliefs,
and...

00:37:34.716 --> 00:37:36.911
We are not immigrants!

00:37:36.951 --> 00:37:43.823
I will not deny 20 million years
of history and Doctrine

00:37:43.858 --> 00:37:48.261
just because one insignificant
saurian has a theory.

00:37:48.296 --> 00:37:51.629
One last time:

00:37:51.666 --> 00:37:54.863
Could you be mistaken?

00:37:54.902 --> 00:37:57.496
It's you who are mistaken,
Minister.

00:37:57.538 --> 00:37:59.199
What?

00:37:59.240 --> 00:38:02.107
You accuse Gegen of having
his objectivity clouded

00:38:02.143 --> 00:38:04.270
by... wishful thinking,

00:38:04.312 --> 00:38:06.576
but aren't you guilty
of the same charge?

00:38:06.614 --> 00:38:09.139
I am not on trial here.

00:38:09.183 --> 00:38:10.445
I understand,

00:38:10.485 --> 00:38:13.249
but, in a way, your beliefs are.

00:38:13.287 --> 00:38:16.313
How you think about yourselves,
your place in the universe...

00:38:16.357 --> 00:38:18.621
that is on trial

00:38:18.659 --> 00:38:20.820
and this isn't the first time.

00:38:20.862 --> 00:38:22.523
What do you mean?

00:38:22.563 --> 00:38:25.259
I've had the opportunity
over the last few days

00:38:25.299 --> 00:38:26.823
to learn something
about your culture...

00:38:26.868 --> 00:38:28.597
your great accomplishments.

00:38:28.636 --> 00:38:30.900
Consider the breakthrough
into transwarp.

00:38:30.938 --> 00:38:33.566
An incredible achievement,
and yet,

00:38:33.608 --> 00:38:36.099
your ancient Doctrine predicted
terrible disasters

00:38:36.144 --> 00:38:37.839
if it were even attempted.

00:38:37.879 --> 00:38:40.746
That held your race back
for millennia

00:38:40.782 --> 00:38:44.548
until someone took a chance
and challenged that prediction.

00:38:44.585 --> 00:38:46.553
They succeeded, and your society

00:38:46.587 --> 00:38:49.112
entered a new chapter
of exploration

00:38:49.157 --> 00:38:51.591
and your Doctrine
was changed accordingly.

00:38:51.626 --> 00:38:53.651
I know from the history
of my own planet

00:38:53.694 --> 00:38:56.185
that change is difficult.

00:38:56.230 --> 00:38:59.927
New ideas are often greeted
with skepticism... even fear.

00:38:59.967 --> 00:39:02.299
But sometimes
those ideas are accepted

00:39:02.336 --> 00:39:04.167
and when they are...

00:39:04.205 --> 00:39:05.695
progress is made.

00:39:05.740 --> 00:39:07.207
Eyes are opened.

00:39:07.241 --> 00:39:11.644
When I open my eyes
to this theory,

00:39:11.679 --> 00:39:15.775
what I see appalls me.

00:39:15.817 --> 00:39:19.116
I see my race fleeing
your wretched planet...

00:39:19.153 --> 00:39:22.088
a group of pathetic refugees

00:39:22.123 --> 00:39:26.059
crawling and scratching
their way across the galaxy,

00:39:26.094 --> 00:39:29.257
stumbling into this domain.

00:39:29.297 --> 00:39:33.927
I see a race with no birthright,
no legacy.

00:39:34.001 --> 00:39:36.435
That is unacceptable.

00:39:36.471 --> 00:39:39.338
I see something very different,
Minister...

00:39:39.373 --> 00:39:42.308
an ancient race of saurians,

00:39:42.343 --> 00:39:44.140
probably the first
intelligent life

00:39:44.178 --> 00:39:46.271
on Earth... surrounded by

00:39:46.314 --> 00:39:48.908
some of the most terrifying
creatures that ever lived.

00:39:48.950 --> 00:39:50.474
And yet, they thrived,

00:39:50.518 --> 00:39:54.648
developed language
and culture and technology.

00:39:54.689 --> 00:39:57.157
And when the planet
was threatened with disaster,

00:39:57.191 --> 00:39:59.819
they boldly launched
themselves into space,

00:39:59.861 --> 00:40:02.329
crossed what must have seemed
like unimaginable distances,

00:40:02.363 --> 00:40:06.129
facing the unknown every day,

00:40:06.167 --> 00:40:09.568
but somehow,
they stayed together,

00:40:09.604 --> 00:40:14.098
kept going with the same courage
that had served them before

00:40:14.142 --> 00:40:16.133
until they reached
this Quadrant,

00:40:16.177 --> 00:40:18.771
where they laid the foundation
of what was to become

00:40:18.813 --> 00:40:21.145
the great Voth culture.

00:40:21.182 --> 00:40:23.150
Deny that past...

00:40:23.184 --> 00:40:27.518
and you deny the struggle and
achievements of your ancestors.

00:40:27.555 --> 00:40:30.251
Deny your origins on Earth...

00:40:30.291 --> 00:40:33.561
and you deny your true heritage.

00:40:48.809 --> 00:40:51.573
Do you retract your claims?

00:40:54.114 --> 00:40:56.173
No.

00:40:56.216 --> 00:40:58.411
I stand by them.

00:40:58.452 --> 00:41:00.545
Very well.

00:41:00.588 --> 00:41:02.522
It is my judgment
you will suffer

00:41:02.556 --> 00:41:05.150
the consequences
of your obstinacy.

00:41:05.192 --> 00:41:08.423
Gegen, you are guilty
of heresy against Doctrine

00:41:08.462 --> 00:41:11.522
and will be placed
on a detention colony.

00:41:11.565 --> 00:41:13.192
For as long as you breathe,

00:41:13.233 --> 00:41:15.963
you will neither teach
nor engage in research.

00:41:16.070 --> 00:41:19.198
Your life
as a scientist has ended.

00:41:20.207 --> 00:41:21.731
As you wish.

00:41:25.012 --> 00:41:27.981
Chakotay
of the Voyager starship,

00:41:28.048 --> 00:41:32.781
you, your Captain and her crew
will join Professor Gegen.

00:41:32.820 --> 00:41:35.186
Why? You have nothing to gain
by imprisoning them.

00:41:35.222 --> 00:41:36.689
Let them go.

00:41:36.724 --> 00:41:38.487
You will spend
the remainder of your lives

00:41:38.525 --> 00:41:39.583
on a detention colony.

00:41:39.627 --> 00:41:41.788
Your ship will be destroyed.

00:41:41.829 --> 00:41:42.921
Minister...

00:41:42.963 --> 00:41:44.931
You will surrender
your vessel immediately,

00:41:44.965 --> 00:41:46.933
and inform your crew
that this judgment...

00:41:46.967 --> 00:41:48.093
Stop this, please!

00:41:51.271 --> 00:41:55.071
Are you offering me
an alternative?

00:42:12.493 --> 00:42:14.586
I have...

00:42:14.628 --> 00:42:16.425
reconsidered

00:42:16.463 --> 00:42:18.727
and I retract my claims

00:42:18.766 --> 00:42:22.429
regarding
the Distant Origin Theory.

00:42:24.271 --> 00:42:29.140
My analysis of the data
was obviously flawed.

00:42:31.545 --> 00:42:34.275
I was...

00:42:34.314 --> 00:42:36.839
mistaken.

00:42:36.884 --> 00:42:39.910
You are prepared to refute
your work publicly

00:42:39.953 --> 00:42:42.080
before the Circles of Science?

00:42:43.824 --> 00:42:45.348
Yes.

00:42:45.392 --> 00:42:48.589
You will then be assigned
to another area of research.

00:42:48.629 --> 00:42:51.655
Surely paleontology
has become tiresome to you

00:42:51.699 --> 00:42:53.326
after so many years.

00:42:53.367 --> 00:42:55.631
Perhaps metallurgical analysis

00:42:55.669 --> 00:42:58.866
would be a more rewarding
vocation for you.

00:42:58.906 --> 00:43:00.999
Perhaps.

00:43:02.276 --> 00:43:04.870
I am not unreasonable.

00:43:04.912 --> 00:43:07.847
You were drawn into this...
situation

00:43:07.881 --> 00:43:10.441
through no fault of your own.

00:43:10.484 --> 00:43:11.951
You are to be returned
to your ship

00:43:12.019 --> 00:43:15.455
where you will set course
away from our territory.

00:43:18.559 --> 00:43:21.119
It would be
in your best interest

00:43:21.161 --> 00:43:24.858
if I never saw you again.

00:43:47.087 --> 00:43:49.521
I'm not so good at chemistry.

00:43:49.556 --> 00:43:52.650
My career
as a metallurgical scientist

00:43:52.693 --> 00:43:56.720
is likely to be...
undistinguished.

00:43:56.764 --> 00:43:58.698
I'm sorry.

00:43:58.732 --> 00:44:01.166
I was foolish.

00:44:03.237 --> 00:44:04.568
Arrogant...

00:44:06.140 --> 00:44:07.664
and I lost everything.

00:44:07.708 --> 00:44:09.733
You were courageous,

00:44:09.777 --> 00:44:11.267
as the Voth have always been

00:44:11.311 --> 00:44:13.302
from the first time
they left Earth.

00:44:15.115 --> 00:44:18.107
And you, Chakotay,
have been a colleague...

00:44:18.152 --> 00:44:19.949
a friend.

00:44:19.987 --> 00:44:22.478
I will not forget you.

00:44:22.523 --> 00:44:25.458
There's something else
I hope you never forget.

00:44:37.738 --> 00:44:39.569
Someday,

00:44:39.606 --> 00:44:42.871
every Voth will see this
as home.

00:44:42.910 --> 00:44:46.368
Someday.
Eyes open.

00:44:46.413 --> 00:44:48.711
Eyes open.

00:44:49.750 --> 00:44:51.615
Chakotay to Voyager.

00:44:51.652 --> 00:44:53.210
Energize.
